{"book":10,"chapter":1,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / GETTING TO KNOW RUST / CHAPTER 1","slides":[{"title":"Welcome","sub":"Chapter 1 · Taking it slow","short":"Intro","main":"Calmly: history, first program, then variables, types, functions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Why this course","What you already know","Plan"],"captions":["Calm and unhurried: language history, a first program, then variables, types, functions, strings and lists","Python and a bit about how computers work — that is enough; we will explain the rest as we go","By the end of this part you will read simple Rust code and write your own"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":180.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Rust: step by step","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"no rush, no fear","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Python\nbasics","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"how the\ncomputer works","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"that is enough","tone":"green","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":60.0,"y":48.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Hello, world","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":48.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Variables","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":300.0,"y":48.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Types","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":60.0,"y":92.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Functions","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":180.0,"y":92.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Strings","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s5","x":300.0,"y":92.0,"w":106.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Lists","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[6.8,26.1]}]},{"title":"What is Rust","sub":"Compiled, typed, no GC","short":"What it is","main":"The speed of low-level languages and the safety of high-level ones — the compiler checks it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Compiled","Statically typed","No garbage collector"],"captions":["Rust is compiled ahead of time: the source becomes a ready-made executable","Static types: the type of every value is known before the program runs","No garbage collector, but no leaks: memory is governed by rules the compiler checks"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"main.rs","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":110.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rustc","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":214.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":252.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"program","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["let age: u8 = 30;","let name: &str = \"Anya\";"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"u8 and &str are known at build time","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"the compiler\ncleans up memory","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"no\ncollector","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.6,28.9]}]},{"title":"Where it came from","sub":"2006 → 2015 → today","short":"History","main":"A personal project in 2006, version 1.0 on May 15, 2015, editions every three years.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["2006–2009","2015: version 1.0","2021 and beyond"],"captions":["2006: Graydon Hoare's personal project at Mozilla; since 2009 Mozilla backs the language — it needs a safe engine for the browser","May 15, 2015: version 1.0 is out; a new version ships every six weeks, and old code keeps compiling","Language editions every three years (2018, 2021, 2024); since 2021 the language belongs to the independent Rust Foundation"],"frames":[[{"t":"line","id":"ax","x1":30.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":330.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"muted","width":2.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2006","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2009","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":90.0,"y":46.0,"text":"personal project","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":240.0,"y":46.0,"text":"Mozilla backing","size":9.0}],[{"t":"line","id":"ax","x1":30.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":330.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"muted","width":2.0},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2015","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":180.0,"y":46.0,"text":"version 1.0 · May 15","tone":"yellow","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"new version every 6 weeks","size":9.0}],[{"t":"line","id":"ax","x1":30.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":330.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"muted","width":2.0},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2018","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":150.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2021","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":230.0,"y":80.0,"w":52.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2024","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":150.0,"y":46.0,"text":"Rust Foundation","tone":"green","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":150.0,"y":118.0,"text":"editions every three years","size":9.0}]],"cues":[16.1,32.5]}]},{"title":"Why it was created","sub":"Memory errors","short":"Why","main":"About 70% of serious vulnerabilities are memory errors; Rust catches them at build time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Memory errors","Share of vulnerabilities","Rules in the compiler"],"captions":["In C and C++: out-of-bounds access, use after free, double free, data races","By Microsoft and Chromium estimates, about 70% of serious vulnerabilities are memory errors","Rust moves the rules into the compiler: dangerous code will not build, and the error shows up on your machine"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"e0","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"out of bounds","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e1","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"freed memory","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e2","x":90.0,"y":90.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"double free","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e3","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"data race","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"bar","id":"a","x":120.0,"y":130.0,"w":60.0,"hh":90.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"red","text":"70%"},{"t":"bar","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":130.0,"w":60.0,"hh":38.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"30%"},{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":120.0,"y":148.0,"text":"memory","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":240.0,"y":148.0,"text":"other","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a~cell","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"build-time\nerror","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b~cell","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"not on the\nuser's side","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":150.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.8,31.7]}]},{"title":"Where it is used","sub":"From browsers to the kernel","short":"Where","main":"Firefox, Android, Windows, clouds, tools, and Linux drivers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Browsers and systems","Clouds and tools","Linux kernel"],"captions":["Parts of Firefox, Android and Windows are written in Rust","Cloud services, databases, command-line tools, game engines, embedded devices, WebAssembly","Since 2022 Rust is allowed in the Linux kernel: drivers are written in it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Firefox","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Android","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Windows","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":62.0,"y":52.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"clouds","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":180.0,"y":52.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"databases","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":298.0,"y":52.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"tools","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":62.0,"y":96.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"games","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b4","x":180.0,"y":96.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"embedded","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b5","x":298.0,"y":96.0,"w":104.0,"h":28.0,"text":"WebAssembly","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"k","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Linux kernel","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"drivers in Rust","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":180.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":104.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[20.3,21.3]}]},{"title":"Compiled ahead of time","sub":"Not an interpreter","short":"Compilation","main":"A ready-made file of machine instructions runs without Rust.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust","Result"],"captions":["Python: the interpreter reads your file line by line on every run","Rust: the compiler turns the code into machine instructions once — the very ones you studied in the architecture book","The finished file can be given to someone else: they need neither Rust nor an interpreter"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"script.py","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":110.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":200.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"interpreter","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":246.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":286.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":320.0,"y":66.0,"w":50.0,"h":30.0,"text":"result","tone":"green","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":30.0,"text":"main.rs","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":92.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":124.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":160.0,"y":66.0,"w":66.0,"h":30.0,"text":"compiler","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":194.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":228.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"machine\ninstructions","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"hello (file)","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":150.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"another computer\nwithout Rust","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.4,22.0]}]},{"title":"rustup and cargo","sub":"Tools","short":"Tools","main":"Two commands: cargo new creates a project, cargo run runs it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["rustup","cargo","Commands"],"captions":["rustup is the installer: it installs the rustc compiler and cargo and can switch versions","cargo is the main helper: it creates a project, builds, runs and fetches dependencies","Two commands are enough: cargo new creates a project, cargo run builds and runs it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"rustup","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":70.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"rustc","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"cargo","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":290.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"versions","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":150.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":70.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":180.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":290.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"cargo","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":56.0,"y":110.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"new","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":138.0,"y":110.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"run","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":220.0,"y":110.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"build","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":302.0,"y":110.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"check","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":144.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":56.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":168.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":192.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":216.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":302.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ cargo new hello","$ cd hello","$ cargo run","Hello, world!"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"plain","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[13.4,25.9]}]},{"title":"First program","sub":"fn main and println!","short":"Hello","main":"main is the entry point; println! is a macro that prints a line.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["fn main","println!","Run"],"captions":["fn declares a function, main is the entry point: execution starts there; the body is in curly braces","println! prints a line and ends it with a newline; the exclamation mark means “macro”; it ends with a semicolon","We ran it — “Hello, world!” appears on screen; the program ends"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn main() {","","}"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn main() {","    println!(\"Hello, world!\");","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["fn main() {","    println!(\"Hello, world!\");","}"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":220.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Hello, world!","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.2,21.8]}]},{"title":"Formatting output","sub":"{} and \\n","short":"println!","main":"{} inserts values; {{ }} prints braces; print! does not add a newline.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Braces {}","Names and {{ }}","print! and \\n"],"captions":["A pair of curly braces in a string is replaced by a value: println!(\"{} + {} = {}\", 2, 3, 5);","Inside the braces you can write a variable name: {name}; two braces in a row — {{ — print one real brace","print! does not add a newline; a newline is written as \\n; \\t is a tab"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["println!(\"{} + {} = {}\", 2, 3, 5);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"2 + 3 = 5","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let name = \"Anya\";","println!(\"Hello, {name}! {{ok}}\");"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":106.0,"w":200.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Hello, Anya! {ok}","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["print!(\"one \");","print!(\"two\\n\");","println!(\"three\");"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":108.0,"w":120.0,"h":40.0,"text":"one two\nthree","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.5,23.2]}]},{"title":"Comments and style","sub":"//, snake_case, cargo fmt","short":"Style","main":"One style for everyone: cargo fmt tidies the code.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Comments","Style","cargo fmt"],"captions":["// comments to the end of the line; /* … */ — several lines; /// — documentation for the next item","Four spaces of indentation; variables and functions in snake_case; types capitalized","cargo fmt brings code to one common style — no more arguing about spaces"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["// this is a comment","/* and this one","   spans several lines */","/// function documentation"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let user_name = \"Anya\";   // snake_case","struct UserCard { }        // capitalized"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"messy code","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":160.0,"y":50.0,"text":"cargo fmt","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"tidy","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.4,27.4]}]},{"title":"Compiler messages","sub":"Reading errors","short":"Errors","main":"Read from the first line: code, phrase, location, and help.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Error","How to read","Hint"],"captions":["Forgot the semicolon — the compiler will not build the program and shows an error","Error code, a clear phrase, an arrow to the file and line, the underlined spot; read from the first line","Often there is a help at the bottom — a hint on how to fix it; rustc --explain E0425 tells you more"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn main() {","    println!(\"hello\")","}"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":320.0,"h":80.0,"text":"error: expected `;`, found `}`\n --> src/main.rs:2:22\n  |\n2 |     println!(\"hello\")\n  |                      ^ help: add `;` here","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"text","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"text":"rustc --explain E0425","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":280.0,"h":40.0,"text":"a detailed explanation with examples\nright in your terminal","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.2,27.0]}]},{"title":"How the course works","sub":"Slides, questions, exercises","short":"Course","main":"Exercises are checked by a real rustc in a sandbox.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Chapters","Exercises","Section map"],"captions":["Every chapter has slides, a voice-over talk, self-check questions and exercises","Exercises are checked by a real rustc in an isolated sandbox; if the code does not build, you see the compiler message","First the introduction (very simple tasks), then comparison with Python, ownership and borrowing, threads, async and a server"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"slides","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"voice-over","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"questions","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"exe